Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.560
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:12.300
Oh my, here is Stable Diffusion version&nbsp;
2. So, what is this? Stable Diffusion is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.700
a free and open source text to image AI,&nbsp;
which means that we write a piece of text,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.620
and it creates exactly that image&nbsp;
for us. All this, for everyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:28.980
for free! So good. And now, here are 10&nbsp;
things you should know about version 2.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:36.480
One, it can now generate images with higher&nbsp;
resolution. More details for free, that sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:44.160
amazing, but, it doesn’t stop there, because two,&nbsp;
it can also perform super resolution better. Super&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:50.880
resolution means that in goes a coarse image,&nbsp;
and out comes a beautiful image with a lot more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:58.560
detail. And when I say a lot, I mean a lot.&nbsp;
Just look at how much better this is. So good.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:05.340
Three, it can also go from depth plus&nbsp;
text to image. What does that mean? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:11.400
we can give it an input image, and then,&nbsp;
it fires up this paper. Oh goodness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.820
that is a powerful paper, it can not only&nbsp;
estimate depth maps for photos really well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:25.140
but get this, it can even imagine if a drawing&nbsp;
were a real photo, and estimate the depth of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:32.340
that. Incredible. So, it creates the depth&nbsp;
map for this image, and using our prompt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:39.240
fills it with information that makes sense. This&nbsp;
is excellent if we wish to just specify the pose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.580
of our hero, and it will generate as many&nbsp;
similar variations for it as we can imagine.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.140
Or, we can also do this. Lots of amazing variants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:54.600
for the same concept. The limit is&nbsp;
only our imagination. Loving it.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:02:00.000
Four, image inpainting is now&nbsp;
easier. This means that we can say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.220
that we wish to retain this part of the&nbsp;
image, and the AI should just fill in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:11.160
rest according to our instructions. This is&nbsp;
super fun, and it will help with one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:17.100
most important things we could all ask for: and&nbsp;
that is quick turnaround times for our ideas.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:23.880
Five, it can now generate more convincing&nbsp;
images of refractive objects. You know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:27.960
I am a light transport researcher&nbsp;
by trade and this makes me very,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:35.700
very happy. Human eyes, and water, underwater&nbsp;
images, not a problem. And some of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

